{"id": "EUVD-2026-101136", "enisaUuid": "605af3c0-b09e-3dbb-8c7c-66d11653d970", "description": "libsmb2 through 6.2 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in smb2_decode_file_fs_volume_info and smb2_decode_file_fs_attribute_info that allows malicious SMB servers to read past reply buffers. Attackers controlling a server or intercepting unsigned sessions can send crafted QUERY_INFO replies with missing or oversized name lengths to crash the client.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T15:01:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T19:49:00", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libsmb2-query-info-reply-oob-read", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2/blob/d67e213a5c4e7e4969fd81f0b95e4ca5831fbba1/lib/smb2-data-filesystem-info.c#L71", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2/commit/dd0bbdee24bb56f7ec95431afc07ce0a666533f7", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libsmb2-through-6.2-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-file-system-info-decoders"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110713", "GHSA-w2j6-hg6c-f9mp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2929948a-6df6-317a-9995-34b368a575c9", "product": {"name": "libsmb2", "vendor": {"name": "sahlberg"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0e9c9756-03e5-3f87-b325-9a620ed7bdac", "vendor": {"name": "sahlberg"}}], "isExploited": false}